  "narrative": "All nine new comparisons have valid cells and signed estimates in the claimed direction. I applied the stated discovery decision rule: accept only when the signed interval lower bound exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units; near-threshold positive results remain unresolved; and do not reject solely because uncertainty prevents threshold acceptance when the direction remains supportive. The four core associations persisted strongly in the lower screen_roc_auc stratum. SMARCA4 loss had signed +0.853, lower +0.757 (R255/H248), supporting stronger dependency. TP53 loss had signed +0.383, lower +0.236 (R256/H249), and KEAP1 loss had signed +0.895, lower +0.802 (R257/H250), both supporting weaker dependency. MSI-high had signed +0.865, lower +0.672 (R258/H251), supporting stronger dependency. These are dataset-specific persistence checks within a constructed screen-quality stratum, not independent replication, and should not be interpreted as causal or externally generalizable. SMARCA4 loss in the median-high research_signature_c stratum also produced a large accepted absolute effect, signed +0.898, lower +0.805 (R261/H254); this supports the presence of a substantial SMARCA4-loss contrast in that stratum but does not establish biological meaning of the constructed assay or convert the earlier unresolved interaction into a confirmed interaction. PTEN remained context-dependent and secondary. Overall PTEN in low screen quality was directionally supportive but subthreshold in uncertainty, signed +0.262, lower +0.125 (R259/H252), so it remains unresolved. In a clean core background excluding MSI-high, TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, and SMARCA4 loss, PTEN loss was accepted at a borderline lower bound, signed +0.266, lower +0.151 (R260/H253). I accept it under the strict lower-bound rule, but its margin is very small and should be treated cautiously. When the already clean background was further restricted to STK11 wildtype, the effect attenuated and became unresolved, signed +0.221, lower +0.097 (R262/H255), underscoring fragility of PTEN conclusions across nested contexts. CDKN2A in a clean low-screen background was directionally positive but below the meaningful-effect threshold, signed +0.112, lower +0.033 (R263/H256); I leave it unresolved rather than overinterpreting a positive but subthreshold contrast. No validation request is possible because voluntary validation capacity is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence map: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high are strongly associated with stronger dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are strongly associated with weaker dependency. All four core associations also cleared the threshold in the lower screen_roc_auc stratum (H248-H251/R255-R258) and therefore have broad dataset-internal robustness, though these strata remain descriptive and noncausal. SMARCA4 also has a strong accepted absolute contrast in median-high research_signature_c (H254/R261), but the earlier relative interaction remains descriptive. PTEN is secondary and context-dependent: overall and low-screen overall PTEN remain unresolved (H252/R259), while clean core low-screen PTEN is accepted only at the borderline lower bound (H253/R260) and further restricting to STK11 wildtype becomes unresolved (H255/R262). CDKN2A remains near/subthreshold and unresolved in clean backgrounds (H247/R254, H256/R263). No voluntary validation requests remain. Future interpretation should treat accepted subgroup results as dataset-specific associations, with special caution for borderline PTEN contexts and constructed-assay strata."
